agent-ops task task-3ca5240c-80d6-482a-8995-5d3a15ed6757: Cut in-session verify and review token burn
intent: Make agents wait for verify/review/batch in one blocking step: print a last-duration wait hint (display-only, git common dir), show failing command stderr tail plus acceptance failure rows and a private redacted log so failures need no suite rerun, and add managed per-harness wait guidance (batch for a single task, subagent wait only as fallback). No change to evidence, gates, review rounds or test suite duration.
criteria:
- verify-failure-detail: When a verification command fails, verify text output shows the redacted last 2KB of that command's stderr (stdout when stderr is empty), each non-PASS acceptance row with criterion, phase, failureClass and failing checkIds, and the path of a private redacted log (at most 64KB) at .agent-ops/tasks/verify-logs/<command-id>.log; batch prints the same lines to stderr for a failing verify; PASS output is unchanged and JSON only gains optional fields. Proven by node tests.
- wait-duration-hint: verify, review (not show or criteria mode) and batch print one stderr line before any work: with a recorded duration for that command in <git-common-dir>/agent-ops/durations.json it states the last elapsed minutes, otherwise only the wait guidance; every run that returns records its elapsed milliseconds there by temp-file rename; any read or write failure leaves the command result, exit code and stdout unchanged. Proven by node tests.
- managed-wait-guidance: Generated managed rules for every harness tell agents to wait for verify/review/batch in one blocking step without status-only messages (CLAUDE.md: run_in_background and wait for the completion notification; AGENTS.md: one sleep of about the printed duration, then check; GEMINI.md: one blocking call), recommend agent-ops batch --parent <task-id> --yes for a single task too, and use a small-context subagent wait only when no duration is printed or the host cannot block; codex and opencode output stay identical; docs/en and docs/zh-TW review spec describe the same. Proven by node tests.
